Nuur's voters, drawn from socially conservative Catholic communities, transferred overwhelmingly to Thea, reflecting the informal alliance between the Christian Socialist Union and the National Party on social issues.

Qaasim's Industrial Party voters split between Thea, who had secured corporate tax reductions through the Industrial Party agreement, and Sahamin, whose technology-friendly policies appealed to business-oriented voters.

Sahamin's voters, representing the rump Forward Party after the Forward Progressive Party split, divided between Xasan and Thea. The Forward Progressive Party faction had already endorsed Xasan during the campaign, contributing to her strong showing among former Forward voters.

Garaad's Socialist Party voters transferred decisively to Xasan, reflecting the coalition alignment between the Socialist Party and progressive parties in opposition to the National Party.

=== Voter turnout ===

Total voter turnout was 72.4 per cent, representing a significant increase from the 68.2 per cent turnout in the [[2025 Burawi leadership election]]. The heightened turnout reflected the contentious nature of the recall process and the historic possibility of electing Burawa's first female Leader.

